r\nGo ahead :+1: ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/2340100549/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/2340105928","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/17834#issuecomment-2340105928","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/17834","id":2340105928,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAD-Lgs6Ley7I","user":{"login":"felixxm","id":2865885,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjU4ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2865885?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxm","html_url":"https://github.com/felixxm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-09-10T09:11:23Z","updated_at":"2024-09-10T09:11:23Z","body":"> Let me know if the changes seems okay\r\n\r\nI didn't have time to check this, but is it work with the minimal support version of `oracledb`, i.e. `1.3.2`, or do we need to bump that requirement.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/2340105928/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/2340162530","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/17834#issuecomment-2340162530","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/17834","id":2340162530,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAD-Lgs6LfAvi","user":{"login":"suraj-ora-2020","id":78541439,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4NTQxNDM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78541439?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020","html_url":"https://github.com/suraj-ora-2020","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-09-10T09:36:21Z","updated_at":"2024-09-10T09:36:43Z","body":"> I didn't have time to check this, but is it work with the minimal support version of `oracledb`, i.e. `1.3.2`, or do we need to bump that requirement.\r\n\r\nSure I will test once and update you.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/2340162530/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/2341686247","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/17834#issuecomment-2341686247","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/17834","id":2341686247,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAD-Lgs6Lk0vn","user":{"login":"suraj-ora-2020","id":78541439,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4NTQxNDM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78541439?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020","html_url":"https://github.com/suraj-ora-2020","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-09-10T18:14:13Z","updated_at":"2024-09-11T02:56:25Z","body":"> I didn't have time to check this, but is it work with the minimal support version of `oracledb`, i.e. `1.3.2`, or do we need to bump that requirement.\r\n\r\n@felixxm I have tested the code. We need to bump the minimum requirement version 2.0.0 as from this version it ensures all the connections are closed before closing the pool (see [this](https://python-oracledb.readthedocs.io/en/latest/release_notes.html#:~:text=Internal%20change%20to%20ensure%20that%20all%20connections%20in%20a%20pool%20have%20been%20closed%20gracefully%20before%20the%20pool%20is%20closed.)).\r\nAlso in 2.3.0 contains major re-work in connection pooling which solves some known issues (see [this](https://python-oracledb.readthedocs.io/en/latest/release_notes.html#:~:text=When%20calling%20ConnectionPool.acquire()%20or%20AsyncConnectionPool.acquire()%2C%20the%20connection%20pool%20mode%20oracledb.POOL_GETMODE_TIMEDWAIT%20now%20always%20honors%20the%20wait_timeout%20value%20and%20the%20connection%20request%20will%20not%20additionally%20be%20delayed%20by%20any%20internal%20network%20ping%20to%20the%20database)).\r\nThe minimum we need is 2.0.0 and best would be 2.3.0. We may as well use 2.4.1 as the minimum version to encourage people to update the driver. What are your thoughts on this?\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/2341686247/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/2341694294","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/17834#issuecomment-2341694294","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/17834","id":2341694294,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAD-Lgs6Lk2tW","user":{"login":"suraj-ora-2020","id":78541439,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4NTQxNDM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78541439?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020","html_url":"https://github.com/suraj-ora-2020","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suraj-ora-2020/events{/privacy}",